# Kitehold Rock: a lollipop on the windy grass plain. Units in metres:
# x east, z south, from the world's north-west corner.
#
# The stick is a long straight west across the plain into the wind, and
# north up its west side. The head spirals up the outside of the basalt
# plug three quarters of the way round, crosses the kite town on its top,
# and leaves the east edge over a lip, where the kart opens a kite and
# glides out over the plain. A dust devil off the sun-warmed rock south of
# the glide lifts a kart that banks into it: more hang time, a bigger kick
# on landing, against the lower, quicker dive straight down onto the road.
# No pads: the wind, the slope and the glide do their work.
track kitehold_rock size 768 style basalt
title KITEHOLD ROCK
blurb A blustery spring day on the grass plain: a long straight into the wind, a spiral round the black rock to the kite town on its top, and a kite glide off its edge back down to the plain.
race laps 3 rivals 5 vehicle kart
road 15.5 bank 1.3
land 30 2
hour 13

